Third-party components and their licenses
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Ultralytics — AGPL-3.0
   https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics

   Ultralytics is NOT a default dependency. A plain `poetry install` produces a
   dependency tree with no AGPL component. It is available as an optional extra
   (`poetry install --extras yolo`) for retraining and for experimenting with
   YOLO segmentation heads.

   Historical note: v1 loaded YOLOv5 at runtime through `torch.hub.load()` and
   shipped `pycnidia-model.pt`, weights produced by training with Ultralytics
   YOLOv5. Ultralytics takes the position that models trained with their
   software are derivative works and inherit the AGPL-3.0 license. Those
   weights are therefore AGPL-3.0, not MIT, wherever they are distributed.

   v2 neither loads nor ships them. The pycnidia detector is being retrained.
   If its replacement is trained with Ultralytics, the resulting weights will
   inherit AGPL-3.0 in the same way, and that will be stated here. Training on
   a non-Ultralytics architecture would remove the constraint entirely.

2. U-Net necrosis weights (`necrosis-model-375.safetensors`, and the 50/100/200/300
   ablation checkpoints)
   Originally trained with the authors' own U-Net implementation
   (https://github.com/maximereder/unet) on TensorFlow/Keras, which is
   Apache-2.0. Converted to PyTorch without retraining; the values are
   unchanged. No copyleft obligation attaches to these weights; they are
   covered by this repository's MIT License.

3. PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), OpenCV (Apache-2.0), NumPy / pandas (BSD-3-Clause),
   safetensors (Apache-2.0).
   These are ordinary runtime dependencies installed from PyPI and are not
   redistributed by this repository.

   TensorFlow was a dependency of v1 only. It has been removed.

